graduate: stamp the pedigree.

```sh
rhx education.pedigree set
```

it reads every course of this pursuit and writes one pedigree entry for $ROLE into
$BRIEFS_DIR/education/, named in $BOOT_PATH.

$GRADUATE_RENDER_STEP

the guard also boots $ROLE as rhachet does. where its boot spec declares a `budget:`, a boot
past it holds this stone: move a `say` entry to `ref`, or raise `budget.tokens` on purpose,
then re-stamp.

then pass this stone. it rests on the review that chose to graduate and the pedigree entry `set`
wrote ($PEDIGREE_ENTRY); no yield file of its own is owed. until the entry stands, the guard's
judge holds the stone and names `set`:

```sh
rhx route.stone.set --stone 4.graduate --as passed
```
